{"id":"resp_a754d5a45d7ed09a","created_at":1795618374,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_80a833eaec650b52","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes representing the requirement TRF-032 clause 4.1: \"If scantlings derived from these regulations are less than those required by the classification society for a ship that has not been ice strengthened, the latter shall be used.\"\n\nWe have ontology terms: classificationSocietyRequiredScantling (property), regulationRequiredScantling, selectedDesignScantling, iceStrengtheningStatus (boolean). Domain for these properties is benchmarkEntity (but termOwners say they belong to ship). The contract owners mapping: owners for each property = ship.\n\nWe need SHACL shape targeting class ship (owner class). The requirement imposes that if ship is not ice strengthened (iceStrengtheningStatus false?) then selectedDesignScantling must be >= classificationSocietyRequiredScantling? Actually the rule: If the scantlings derived from regulations are less than those required by classification society for a ship that has not been ice strengthened, the latter shall be used. Means: when iceStrengtheningStatus = false (not ice strengthened), and regulationRequiredScantling < classificationSocietyRequiredScantling, then selectedDesignScantling must be set to classificationSocietyRequiredScantling (or at least not less than that). In SHACL we can enforce that selectedDesignScantling >= classificationSocietyRequiredScantling when iceStrengtheningStatus false. The condition \"if regulationRequiredScantling is less than classificationSocietyRequiredScantling\" is essentially implied by the comparison. Could implement a rule: when iceStrengtheningStatus = false, enforce selectedDesignScantling >= classificationSocietyRequiredScantling. Optionally also ensure that selectedDesignScantling = max(regulationRequiredScantling, classificationSocietyRequiredScantling). In SHACL we can't compute max, but we can use a SPARQL constraint: selectedDesignScantling = IF(regulationRequiredScantling > classificationSocietyRequiredScantling, regulationRequiredScantling, classificationSocietyRequiredScantling). Simpler: enforce selectedDesignScantling >= classificationSocietyRequiredScantling and selectedDesignScantling >= regulationRequiredScantling; i.e., selected must be at least both. That satisfies rule.\n\nSHACL shape should use quantityEncoding: numericValue and unit predicate.\n\nWe need to specify path to selectedDesignScantling etc. Probably they are object properties linking ship to QuantityValue nodes. The QuantityValue nodes have numericValue and unit.\n\nThus shape: sh:targetClass ship. Then sh:property for iceStrengtheningStatus: datatype xsd:boolean.\n\nThen conditional constraints using sh:if (SHACL 2.0?) There is sh:or? Might use sh:condition with SPARQL. Use sh:sparql for constraint: \"FILTER (!?iceStatus || (?regScant < ?classScant && ?selected >= ?classScant))\". Better: If iceStrengtheningStatus true => no constraint. If false => selected >= class. Not need compare reg vs class; just selected must be >= class.\n\nThus SPARQL query: SELECT ... WHERE { ?this a ship . OPTIONAL { ?this iceStrengtheningStatus ?ice . } OPTIONAL { ?this regulationRequiredScantling ?reg . ?reg qudt:numericValue ?regVal . ?reg qudt:unit ?unit1 . } OPTIONAL { ?this classificationSocietyRequiredScantling ?cls . ?cls qudt:numericValue ?clsVal . ?cls qudt:unit ?unit2 . } OPTIONAL { ?this selectedDesignScantling ?sel . ?sel qudt:numericValue ?selVal . ?sel qudt:unit ?unit3 . } FILTER ( (bound(?ice) && ?ice = false) && (bound(?clsVal) && (!bound(?selVal) || ?selVal < ?clsVal) ) ) }.\n\nIf any violation, raise sh:NodeConstraintViolation.\n\nWe need to include prefixes: sh, xsd, qudt, vocab.\n\nProvide SHACL graph in Turtle.\n\nAlso include statements linking properties to classes? Not needed.\n\nWe'll include sh:severity sh:Violation.\n\nNow produce final answer with <BEGIN_SHACL> line then Turtle then <END_SHACL>.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_b777030534c79814","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .\n\n# Shape targeting all ships (the admitted synthetic population)\nex:ShipScantlingShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    \n    # Ice strengthening status (boolean) – optional but used in the conditional rule\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:iceStrengtheningStatus ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;\n        sh:name \"Ice strengthening status\" ;\n        sh:description \"True if the ship is ice‑strengthened, false otherwise.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Regulation‑derived scantling (QuantityValue)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:regulationRequiredScantling ;\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n        sh:name \"Regulation required scantling\" ;\n        sh:description \"Scantlings obtained from the Ice Class Regulations.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Classification‑society required scantling for a non‑ice‑strengthened ship (QuantityValue)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:classificationSocietyRequiredScantling ;\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n        sh:name \"Classification‑society required scantling\" ;\n        sh:description \"Scantlings required by the classification society for a ship without ice strengthening.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Selected design scantling (QuantityValue) – the value that must satisfy the rule\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:selectedDesignScantling ;\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n        sh:name \"Selected design scantling\" ;\n        sh:description \"The scantling actually used in the ship design.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Conditional SPARQL constraint enforcing the requirement:\n    # If the ship is NOT ice‑strengthened (iceStrengtheningStatus = false) and the\n    # regulation‑derived scantling is less than the classification‑society scantling,\n    # then the selected design scantling must be at least the classification‑society scantling.\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"For a non‑ice‑strengthened ship, the selected design scantling must be ≥ the classification‑society required scantling.\" ;\n        sh:prefixes [\n            sh:declare [\n                sh:prefix \"vocab\" ;\n                sh:namespace \"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#\" ;\n            ] ,\n            sh:declare [\n                sh:prefix \"qudt\" ;\n                sh:namespace \"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/\" ;\n            ] ,\n            sh:declare [\n                sh:prefix \"xsd\" ;\n                sh:namespace \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#\" ;\n            ]\n        ] ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            SELECT $this\n            WHERE {\n                # Retrieve ice‑strengthening status (if present)\n                OPTIONAL { $this vocab:iceStrengtheningStatus ?iceStatus . }\n                \n                # Retrieve regulation‑derived scantling and its numeric value\n                OPTIONAL {\n                    $this vocab:regulationRequiredScantling ?regScantling .\n                    ?regScantling qudt:numericValue ?regVal .\n                    ?regScantling qudt:unit ?regUnit .\n                }\n                \n                # Retrieve classification‑society scantling and its numeric value\n                OPTIONAL {\n                    $this vocab:classificationSocietyRequiredScantling ?clsScantling .\n                    ?clsScantling qudt:numericValue ?clsVal .\n                    ?clsScantling qudt:unit ?clsUnit .\n                }\n                \n                # Retrieve selected design scantling and its numeric value\n                OPTIONAL {\n                    $this vocab:selectedDesignScantling ?selScantling .\n                    ?selScantling qudt:numericValue ?selVal .\n                    ?selScantling qudt:unit ?selUnit .\n                }\n                \n                # Apply the rule only when iceStrengtheningStatus is explicitly false\n                FILTER ( bound(?iceStatus) && ?iceStatus = false )\n                \n                # Both classification‑society and selected scantlings must be present for the check\n                FILTER ( bound(?clsVal) && bound(?selVal) )\n                \n                # Ensure unit compatibility (if units are present they must match)\n                FILTER ( (!bound(?regUnit) || !bound(?clsUnit) || ?regUnit = ?clsUnit) )\n                FILTER ( (!bound(?selUnit) || !bound(?clsUnit) || ?selUnit = ?clsUnit) )\n                \n                # If regulation scantling is less than classification‑society scantling,\n                # enforce selected ≥ classification‑society\n                FILTER ( (!bound(?regVal) || ?regVal >= ?clsVal) ||\n                         (bound(?regVal) && ?regVal < ?clsVal && ?selVal >= ?clsVal) )\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n        sh:severity sh:Violation ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":33697,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":33104,"input_tokens_per_turn":[33697],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1999,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":876,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1999],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":35696},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}